  "notes": "Metres, Z up, robot front -X, shared bottom-centre frame; applied transforms. CPU Cycles 64 diffuse colour times mix(1, AO, 0.6); PBR source retained. Inspection render 1024 square; preview thumbnail 512 for the unchanged validator. 32 shaft facets replace the listed 24: R9 at 24 facets has 0.077 mm chord error, exceeding the binding 0.05 mm tolerance; 32 gives 0.04334 mm and 64 vertices. V clamps use three convex pieces each to preserve the groove. Lead-in is 4 mm axial length at 30 degrees to the shaft axis. No overhead crossbeam. Buttons and station lamp are separate functional parts; scene implements the 0.5 s interlock. Simulator must honor cap/support collision_exclusions for the full 6 mm button stroke. Task 13 compact OBJ exception: positions use 5 decimal metres where safe; necessary vertices retain up to 6 decimals to preserve nonzero triangles, strict collision convexity and the 0.005 mm Euclidean movement bound. Independent fixed-5 rounding cannot satisfy all three. Normals/UVs use 4 decimals; every original triangle, position index and per-corner attribute value is retained. Equal rounded UV records share indices and visual OBJ indices use shorter equivalent relative notation. No collision remeshing, reindexing or simplification. Shaft/chamfer collision coordinates retain 12 decimal metres after compaction and an inward 0.00001 mm numerical guard; vertices never exceed the design circle. This prevents 5-decimal rounding from creating an oversized shaft.",
